WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.200
Next question today is from Lopez Lopez says,
won't businesses just move to other countries

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:12.070
if we increase taxes on them? Basically the
answer is no, not in any statistically significant

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.730
way. This is a very common Cannard that's
floated by the anti tax right in the United

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.770
States and maybe also in in Europe, although
I followed that less closely.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:28.190
The idea here is if you are a corporation,
um, and the government increases your taxes,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:33.720
you would be incentivized to move your operation
to some other country that has a lower tax

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.560
rate. There's a couple of things that we have
to discuss there, but let's start with the

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:44.230
sort of most basic, I mean, American companies,
mostly our American. Yes, there are multinationals

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:49.630
which already are doing business all over
the world and they can more easily move their

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.280
headquarters if not all physical presence.
But what you have to remember is a lot of

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.450
those companies have already established all
sorts of tax shelters and havens. So that's

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:04.439
not going to dramatically change if they've
already determined, well we do better by having

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:09.290
an Irish headquarters, but we still have the
American presence because we have the United

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:14.320
States is such a major market. Um, that is
one reason why they are not going to say we're

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.800
going to relinquish our position in the United
States altogether.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.800
The other thing you have to remember is even
though you might be able to avoid some American

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:29.230
business taxes, if you move your operation
to another country, um, then you risk having

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.850
added tariffs if you still want to do business
with American consumers and corporations.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:40.720
And that in some cases may end up sort of
zeroing out the tax benefit. But most importantly,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.680
all but the biggest businesses are simply
not going to move to other countries. If you

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:50.640
consider all small businesses and even most
medium size businesses that operate primarily

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.200
in the United States, uh, if you have a huge
roofing company or a construction company,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.210
not like a local construction company, but
the big real estate companies and you basically

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:05.340
work in the u s why are you going to move
to another country? It doesn't make any sense.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:11.800
Uh, it's logistically, uh, significant. Uh,
it's a, it's a logistically significant undertaking

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.230
and you're an American company with American
customers and all Americans speaking, uh,

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.709
American English speaking employees.

00:02:18.709 --> 00:02:23.500
So it's just not practical to think that that's
what people are going to do. Now the, we actually

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.530
have some data where we can analyze this because
the same claim has been made for a really

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:35.069
long time about rich people. It's easier for
a rich person to move to another country or

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:41.580
to a lower tax state than it is for a huge
company to move from one country to another.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.930
And it turns out that millionaires don't move
very much. Millionaires actually move way

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:53.360
less than poor people. About half the rate.
Only 2.4% of millionaires move in any given

00:02:53.360 --> 00:03:00.650
year versus 4.5% of poorer Americans. And
interestingly, when millionaires do decide

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:07.650
to move, they slightly favor lower tax states.
Slightly many millionaires are moving to higher

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:12.450
tax states. Many millionaires moved to the
states with the same level of tax and some

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:19.430
millionaires moved to lower tax states and
for 85% of them, the tax rate in the state

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:23.739
they are moving to is not an important consideration.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:29.680
If you go from looking at millionaires to
looking at billionaires, 84% of billionaires

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:35.410
live in their country of birth period, and
there's no solid evidence that tax rates are

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.230
influencing them in terms of where it is that
they want to live. But here's the really important

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:46.390
part. 84% of of billionaires live in their
birth country. 16% of billionaires don't live

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:53.360
in their birth country, but almost all of
them moved to that country before they were

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.280
billionaires. Meaning that if the tax rate
was a consideration, it was a consideration

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:04.950
in some vague, distant way. If they ever are
billionaires, they'd be better off in one

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:10.000
country versus another rather than, I'm moving
now because I want to save money on taxes.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.609
So of course when you get to the margins you
have to consider if a government puts ridiculously

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:22.800
high taxes on corporations, it is going to
serve as more of an incentive to move country

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.580
for that reason.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:29.680
What we're talking about in the United States
about eliminating loopholes and write offs

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.159
and some of these other mechanisms that exist
for corporations to end up paying almost no

00:04:34.159 --> 00:04:38.979
taxes or sometimes no taxes or even getting
tax credits even though they made profit.

00:04:38.979 --> 00:04:44.650
Uh, for the most part, these are changes well
within the sort of reasonable that are not

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:50.909
going to cause a, those businesses to relocate.
I'm sure you can find individual instances

00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:56.240
of anything in a country of 330 million people.
Uh, but from a macro economic level, it's

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:56.800
been widely, widely debunked.

